    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Photographic surveys are an equitable and accessible tool for research and teaching. After minimal training, these photographs, conducted along transects in the rocky intertidal zone, can be be analyzed by anyone, anywhere. These surveys have the potential to become an interactive teaching tool that introduces students to the scientific method in the context of intertidal ecosystems.\r\n\r\nThis deposit contains photoquadrats, data, and metadata from sampling conducted in tbd. \r\n\r\nThis work was conceived in the context of the DIMES (Diversifying and Integrating Marine Education at Stations) program funded by an NSF RCN-UBE Incubator award (2018116). ",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "tbd, t. (2022). DIMES rocky intertidal photographic surveys: region TBD. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/ww861fh0810. https://doi.org/10.25740/ww861fh0810.",
